  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the /llms.txt proposal by Jeremy Howard (Answer.AI, llmstxt.org): the file at /llms.txt or any subpath and its path scope, the structure (optional BOM, required H1, blockquote summary, heading-free details, H2 file lists of [name](url): notes items), the Optional section convention, markdown page versions (page.html.md, page.md, index.html.md, index.md), discovery through rel=alternate type=text/markdown and rel=describedby links or Link headers (RFC 8288), the reference parser and llms_txt2ctx, the Lighthouse audit, and how agents consume the file. It states plainly that llms.txt is a proposal, not a standard or a crawler permission mechanism. Version lines: llms.txt v2 (August 2026) is current with posture build, and llms.txt v1 (2024) is legacy with upgrade steps. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, format, authoring and markdown pages, and validation.",
